&lt;p&gt;As an Electronics Engineer, you will be a member of our interdisciplinary hardware engineering team, contributing to the design and development of electronics for our next-generation drone platforms. You’ll work on electronic modules such as flight controllers, sensors, and vision systems, supporting PCB development from concept through production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of a cross-functional team, you will contribute to advanced systems such as interceptor and reconnaissance drones with integrated visual navigation, as well as quadcopters for defense applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, prototype, and validate avionics PCBs, sensors, and electronic modules for drone platforms, contributing to designs from initial concepts through detailed design and manufacturing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support PCB and product verification activities, including test planning, execution, and documentation; contribute to electrical and mechanical validation such as EMI/EMC compliance testing, thermal cycling, and mechanical shock testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain technical documentation, including design concepts, schematics and CAD drawings, bills of materials (BOMs), assembly instructions, and repair documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with test engineering, manufacturing, and production teams to support the transition of hardware designs from development to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with hardware and software engineers to define electronics requirements, system interfaces, and design solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support troubleshooting and design improvements based on test results, production feedback, and field performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development and improvement of engineering processes and best practices within the hardware team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Electrical or Electronics Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in PCB design and electronic product development, including prototyping, layout, and testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of mixed-signal PCB design, signal integrity, and power integrity principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with PCB testing and troubleshooting, including basic EMC considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Altium Designer is highly desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-power applications, ESCs, and lithium batteries is an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on, solution-oriented mindset with a proactive approach to problem-solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively as part of a cross-functional hardware/software team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good problem-solving and communication skills, with a willingness to learn and take ownership of assigned tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CH/EU citizenship required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Car parking&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellbeing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>
